WEBVTT

00:00:06.291 --> 00:00:08.250
-<i>Good morning.</i>
-<i>Morning.</i>

00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:26.916
Huh?

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:37.916
<i>Huh? What's going on?</i>

00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:39.791
Huh? Mom?

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:42.833
Huh?

00:00:43.791 --> 00:00:45.708
Who might you be?

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.958
Uh, uh.

00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:54.958
Oh, uh… Well, um…
Hello, it's nice to meet you.

00:00:55.458 --> 00:00:57.958
-You must be Hyeong-seok's mother.
-Um. Yes.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:02.791
He's told me a lot about you.
I'm Hyeong-seok's new friend.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.375
Oh, really? Hyeong-seok's friend?
Uh. Welcome. Hyeong-seok, wake up.

00:01:08.875 --> 00:01:10.708
Don't wake him up!

00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:11.708
Huh?

00:02:50.666 --> 00:02:53.375
You two have been living together?

00:02:53.958 --> 00:02:56.166
Yeah, to save on rent and stuff.

00:02:56.791 --> 00:02:59.083
You two live here? It's so small.

00:02:59.666 --> 00:03:02.750
Oh, it actually works well
once you get used to it, that is.

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:06.833
He never mentioned
any of this to me on the phone.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.833
Oh, he must have been so busy
with his part-time job that he forgot.

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:13.208
Part-time job?

00:03:13.833 --> 00:03:16.708
-Hyeong-seok has a job?
-Huh? Oh…

00:03:17.666 --> 00:03:19.166
Uh. Yeah.

00:03:19.916 --> 00:03:21.916
He works the night shift
at a convenience store.

00:03:22.083 --> 00:03:23.833
Oh!

00:03:24.208 --> 00:03:27.416
That must be why he's sleeping so deep.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:31.416
He always takes a deep nap
before he goes to work for the night.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.208
He got himself a job.

00:03:34.916 --> 00:03:37.708
I can't believe it.

00:03:38.708 --> 00:03:39.583
Huh?

00:03:42.166 --> 00:03:43.875
He's gotten so thin.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:51.625
Do you have a minute to chat with me?

00:03:51.958 --> 00:03:54.208
I'd like to get to know you a little.

00:04:17.166 --> 00:04:20.708
Good afternoon…

00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:25.541
You come to places like this a lot?

00:04:26.083 --> 00:04:28.416
Oh, well, from time to time.

00:04:29.916 --> 00:04:31.333
The prices are reasonable…

00:04:31.583 --> 00:04:33.208
…and it's quiet, so we can talk.

00:04:34.166 --> 00:04:35.083
Come on.

00:04:35.416 --> 00:04:38.291
I have to say you must be very popular.

00:04:38.916 --> 00:04:40.958
Hyeong-seok must be so jealous.

00:04:41.458 --> 00:04:45.208
Okay, so, what would you like?

00:04:45.791 --> 00:04:48.208
Well, I'm not really too sure.

00:04:48.541 --> 00:04:51.625
I've never been to a place
quite this nice.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.375
-Heavens!
-Huh?

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.083
DOUBLE ESPRESSO CHIP 4,100 WON
CARAMEL 4,100 WON

00:04:55.208 --> 00:04:56.958
I can't believe how much

00:04:57.041 --> 00:04:58.875
-they charge for a coffee.
-Pardon?

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.958
-I'll just have a glass of water.
-Uh…

00:05:02.791 --> 00:05:06.000
Oh, but it's really no problem. I could…

00:05:15.083 --> 00:05:16.625
Wow!

00:05:16.708 --> 00:05:19.375
So, this is what's called an "Americano"?

00:05:20.083 --> 00:05:22.041
It's good.

00:05:22.625 --> 00:05:26.416
I've only ever had instant coffee sticks
and canned coffee before.

00:05:27.583 --> 00:05:31.541
I wonder if Hyeong-seok has tried this.
I'm sure he'd like it.

00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:34.458
-Oh, right.
-Hmm?

00:05:34.541 --> 00:05:37.291
-I forgot to ask you your name.
-Oh, right.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.291
Well, actually,
my name is Hyeong-seok too.

00:05:41.625 --> 00:05:43.875
Goodness! What a coincidence, huh?

00:05:44.291 --> 00:05:47.833
And now that I think about it
you look a lot like my son too.

00:05:48.416 --> 00:05:51.166
Right.

00:05:52.416 --> 00:05:54.333
I can't believe my Hyeong-seok

00:05:54.416 --> 00:05:55.916
has a good-looking friend

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.708
like you.

00:05:57.875 --> 00:05:59.916
I know
he's a little heavy now,

00:05:59.958 --> 00:06:03.750
but he was such a smart
and handsome little boy when he was young.

00:06:05.875 --> 00:06:07.500
And have you ever heard him sing?

00:06:07.708 --> 00:06:09.083
Oh. Uh. Well…

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:12.083
<i>The new student?</i>

00:06:12.166 --> 00:06:15.666
My son's a wonderful singer.

00:06:15.833 --> 00:06:19.666
I always tell him
that he can really sing.

00:06:19.791 --> 00:06:21.166
Yeah.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.875
That's his friend's mom.

00:06:25.625 --> 00:06:27.083
Behave yourself today.

00:06:27.291 --> 00:06:29.541
They'll fire me
if you start a ruckus in here.

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:35.583
So, that's interesting.
Hyeong-seok got a job then.

00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:38.250
Is it because he needs more money?

00:06:38.833 --> 00:06:40.458
I don't think that's the reason.

00:06:41.083 --> 00:06:43.833
-Has he been eating well?
-Yeah.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:48.208
He brings home extra bread and bento boxes
from the convenience store where he works.

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:50.750
Thanks to him, I get to have some too.

00:06:51.333 --> 00:06:54.291
-<i>He works at a convenience store.</i>
-Really?

00:06:54.583 --> 00:06:57.500
Ah. That job sounds really nice.

00:06:58.875 --> 00:07:02.208
About Hyeong-seok…

00:07:03.208 --> 00:07:06.166
He's not getting bullied or anything,
is he?

00:07:06.875 --> 00:07:07.750
Pardon?

00:07:08.208 --> 00:07:14.791
The truth is… he was bullied a lot
at the school he went to before.

00:07:15.416 --> 00:07:19.375
I was so busy making ends meet each day
that I had no idea,

00:07:19.458 --> 00:07:21.875
even though all I ever thought about was

00:07:22.333 --> 00:07:25.458
how to make things better
for Hyeong-seok.

00:07:26.291 --> 00:07:29.458
I'm a pathetic mother.

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:33.291
<i>Pathetic?</i>
<i>Why would you say that?</i>

00:07:34.583 --> 00:07:35.791
Hyeong-seok is…

00:07:37.875 --> 00:07:40.625
…getting along great with his friends.

00:07:41.666 --> 00:07:43.791
Don't worry so much.

00:07:44.083 --> 00:07:47.541
Oh, is that so? I'm so glad to hear that.

00:07:58.166 --> 00:07:59.500
Oh, miss, are you okay?

00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:01.625
What was that?

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.833
-Would you please just behave yourself?
-More milk.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.583
Another cup.

00:08:07.041 --> 00:08:11.250
Hyeong-seok is so lucky
to have such a good friend like you.

00:08:12.875 --> 00:08:13.750
Oh, I'm…

00:08:14.333 --> 00:08:16.083
<i>Is it my fault that we're poor?</i>

00:08:16.916 --> 00:08:19.166
<i>I mean, what have you ever done</i>
<i>for me anyway?</i>

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:23.416
I am not… a good friend.

00:08:23.916 --> 00:08:26.666
Ah. No. I'm sure you are.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:30.250
I'm so happy you're his friend.
He needs that.

00:08:30.833 --> 00:08:34.333
He calls that a friendship?

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:41.583
My goodness, I think I've taken up
far too much of your time.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.375
-Oh, not at all.
-Excuse me!

00:08:43.458 --> 00:08:46.541
-Yes, ma'am!
-Huh? I know him.

00:08:46.958 --> 00:08:49.666
-What can I get you?
-Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:08:50.458 --> 00:08:53.083
But would you mind,
if I take those boxes over there?

00:08:53.291 --> 00:08:54.333
Oh.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.625
We have someone who usually comes in
for 'em, but sure, go ahead.

00:09:03.666 --> 00:09:07.750
-Are you taking all of these with you?
-Yeah.

00:09:08.208 --> 00:09:11.458
I'm going home so I might as well.

00:09:11.958 --> 00:09:13.791
-I hope I get a seat on the subway.
-Oh.

00:09:13.958 --> 00:09:15.958
<i>How is she</i>
<i>taking all this on the subway?</i>

00:09:16.041 --> 00:09:18.166
I'm embarrassing myself in front of you.

00:09:18.625 --> 00:09:20.333
I'm collecting scrap for money.

00:09:21.166 --> 00:09:24.916
-I just couldn't pass these beauties by.
-<i>Scrap?</i>

00:09:25.708 --> 00:09:27.375
<i>What happened to her old job?</i>

00:09:28.083 --> 00:09:32.375
It's my side job.
Hyeong-seok needs me to send money.

00:09:33.833 --> 00:09:36.750
I haven't told him
that I'm working two jobs yet.

00:09:37.208 --> 00:09:40.375
-You'll keep it a secret, won't you?
-Of course.

00:09:41.583 --> 00:09:44.583
I don't know why,
but I want to tell you everything.

00:09:45.041 --> 00:09:47.166
-You feel so familiar for some reason.
-Oh.

00:09:48.666 --> 00:09:50.458
-Here.
-Huh?

00:09:50.708 --> 00:09:52.458
For the Americano.

00:09:52.541 --> 00:09:54.041
Oh, no, it's quite all right.

00:09:54.208 --> 00:09:56.500
Besides, I've got my own money.

00:09:57.125 --> 00:10:00.416
Would you take this?
Take it for Hyeong-seok's sake.

00:10:00.916 --> 00:10:02.791
-Go ahead, take it.
-Oh.

00:10:04.041 --> 00:10:07.250
I want the two of you
to get along together.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.833
Please, he needs that.

00:10:15.666 --> 00:10:18.375
Okay, then. Thank you, ma'am.

00:10:21.625 --> 00:10:24.750
Hyeong-seok… don't worry about him.

00:10:33.166 --> 00:10:35.000
Oh, I'm so sorry. Gosh, I'm sorry.

00:10:35.375 --> 00:10:39.166
Sorry, sorry, sorry, super sorry.
I'm so, so sorry.

00:10:40.083 --> 00:10:42.375
You don't
wanna see Hyeong-seok before you leave?

00:10:43.375 --> 00:10:46.083
No, I just came to bring him
some food I made.

00:10:46.541 --> 00:10:49.250
I hope he won't be angry
that I brought him food

00:10:49.375 --> 00:10:52.083
-when he's trying to lose weight.
-Oh, of course not.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:55.291
-I'm sure he'll love it.
-You think so?

00:10:55.916 --> 00:11:01.583
I think he appreciates you even more now
that he's living away from you.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:04.875
Ah. I'm so glad to hear that.

00:11:05.458 --> 00:11:09.500
And I can bring more next time
so there'll be enough for both of you.

00:11:09.666 --> 00:11:10.916
Something delicious.

00:11:11.708 --> 00:11:13.166
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:26.708 --> 00:11:27.875
-Hey.
-Huh?

00:11:30.375 --> 00:11:34.041
I saw everything, you jerk.

00:11:34.541 --> 00:11:37.958
Yup, must be karma
for something awful I did in my past life.

00:11:54.875 --> 00:11:57.666
-You're real rotten, aren't you?
-Huh?

00:11:58.208 --> 00:12:00.458
Prepare to get beaten to a pulp.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:01.666
Hmm.

00:12:01.958 --> 00:12:04.500
-Take off your blazer.
-Wha… what?

00:12:05.375 --> 00:12:07.833
-Why?
-You're bullying and using the kid

00:12:07.916 --> 00:12:10.291
as your errand boy, and you lied too.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.541
You're unforgivable!

00:12:13.541 --> 00:12:15.833
I'll never forgive you.

00:12:16.916 --> 00:12:18.541
Sorry?

00:12:23.708 --> 00:12:25.166
<i>I can't believe he dodged that.</i>

00:12:25.541 --> 00:12:28.500
Why? What's up? I don't get it.

00:12:29.541 --> 00:12:31.583
I… I think
there's been a misunderstanding.

00:12:31.708 --> 00:12:34.500
You're despicable. Don't make excuses.

00:12:40.333 --> 00:12:42.333
<i>Does he have hammers for fists?</i>

00:12:42.416 --> 00:12:44.083
<i>He's fast…</i>

00:12:44.166 --> 00:12:45.875
<i>…and powerful.</i>

00:12:45.958 --> 00:12:47.041
<i>He dodged my punch?</i>

00:12:47.125 --> 00:12:49.458
<i>Has he been training to fight</i>
<i>as long as I have?</i>

00:12:52.083 --> 00:12:53.750
<i>If he hits me--</i>

00:12:56.416 --> 00:12:58.208
<i>I'm dead!</i>

00:13:01.833 --> 00:13:05.416
Why are you doing this?

00:13:08.375 --> 00:13:10.875
<i>He's extorting money</i>
<i>from adults too.</i>

00:13:11.541 --> 00:13:13.125
What have I ever done to you?

00:13:13.666 --> 00:13:16.083
<i>I'm gonna give that money</i>
<i>back to the kid.</i>

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.958
Give me the money that the lady gave you,
right now.

00:13:23.333 --> 00:13:25.250
<i>He was watching us just now?</i>

00:13:26.083 --> 00:13:29.041
<i>So, he is trying to take my money.</i>

00:13:29.208 --> 00:13:30.583
<i>You're a little short.</i>

00:13:31.625 --> 00:13:34.166
<i>You're no different</i>
<i>from them after all.</i>

00:13:35.791 --> 00:13:38.208
I…

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:45.000
I will never ever give you this money.

00:13:46.791 --> 00:13:48.833
All right, come on, then.

00:14:01.541 --> 00:14:03.583
<i>He's fast.</i>

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.125
<i>Always go for the gut</i>
<i>when you strike first.</i>

00:14:21.208 --> 00:14:23.208
Huh?

00:14:29.291 --> 00:14:32.000
This stance is the result
of all my training.

00:14:32.916 --> 00:14:36.000
It is the optimal stance to weather blows
from my opponents.

00:14:36.541 --> 00:14:40.333
This stance means,
"I will never fall to someone like you."

00:14:42.083 --> 00:14:44.166
<i>Wh… what do I do?</i>

00:14:45.166 --> 00:14:47.500
Keep your fist right by your cheek
to guard yourself.

00:14:51.416 --> 00:14:56.333
Feet shoulder width apart,
arms parallel, low center of gravity.

00:14:56.833 --> 00:15:01.291
Boxing, huh? Bring it on!

00:15:04.041 --> 00:15:06.083
<i>Now, take a step forward,</i>

00:15:06.541 --> 00:15:08.750
<i>and shift my weight from my hips</i>

00:15:08.833 --> 00:15:11.375
<i>to my shoulders and then to my fists.</i>

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:14.958
<i>This is a straight!</i>

00:15:15.375 --> 00:15:16.833
<i>I've got him.</i>

00:15:27.458 --> 00:15:29.791
Basco!
Oh, why doesn't he ever listen to me…

00:15:41.791 --> 00:15:42.833
Basco…

00:15:47.708 --> 00:15:50.041
I'm sorry,
but could you take care of him?

00:15:50.416 --> 00:15:52.416
Basco.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:01.500
My timing was perfect, but…

00:16:02.583 --> 00:16:04.958
<i>I've got him.</i>

00:16:14.916 --> 00:16:16.500
<i>A spinning back elbow?</i>

00:16:17.291 --> 00:16:20.375
<i>He's well versed in Muay Thai too.</i>

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.625
Park Beom-jae, I have been defeated.

00:16:31.625 --> 00:16:36.750
<i>No.</i>
<i>Burn Knuckle can't lose. You cannot lose.</i>

00:16:50.375 --> 00:16:54.666
<i>How did I win against Basco?</i>

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:58.166
<i>My body moved on its own.</i>

00:16:58.291 --> 00:16:59.666
Huh?

00:17:00.416 --> 00:17:01.833
Welcome, sir…

00:17:06.416 --> 00:17:09.500
<i>Uh. Oh, that must hurt.</i>

00:17:11.708 --> 00:17:12.708
BANANA FLAVORED

00:17:12.875 --> 00:17:14.333
-I'm sorry.
-Huh?

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.958
I couldn't get the money back.

00:17:22.791 --> 00:17:25.125
-Kid.
-Huh? Yeah?

00:17:25.416 --> 00:17:28.458
You're not a weakling. You should train.

00:17:30.708 --> 00:17:32.125
<i>What was that about?</i>

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.166
24+ CONVENIENCE STORE

00:17:35.958 --> 00:17:40.458
<i>Kid… you are strong.</i>

00:17:50.916 --> 00:17:52.750
<i>You belong</i>
<i>on the bottom rung</i>

00:17:53.166 --> 00:17:55.333
<i>until the day you die, you piece of shit.</i>

00:17:56.333 --> 00:17:59.041
I have to get stronger.

00:17:59.791 --> 00:18:04.166
<i>I'm too weak now. I have to get stronger.</i>

00:18:24.416 --> 00:18:26.791
Wel… welcome.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.458
Oh, what's that smell?

00:18:29.708 --> 00:18:32.083
I… I was just…

00:18:38.583 --> 00:18:39.791
Here we go.

00:18:39.916 --> 00:18:41.833
It's 3,000 won.

00:18:44.791 --> 00:18:48.791
-Huh? Wait, why are you…
-Cheers to your workout.

00:19:06.166 --> 00:19:10.375
All right. Sit-ups this time!

00:19:13.958 --> 00:19:16.833
<i>Oh, I can't!</i>

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:20.375
<i>My belly's in the way.</i>
<i>I don't think I can do sit-ups.</i>
